phi-runtime (0.2.1~git202609080954.89ef738-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * A callback outlives the handle it retires. Resetting a timer or an fd
    watch from inside its own callback - a socket class closing its
    descriptor, a repeating poll stopping itself - erased the map node the
    running std::function lived in, freeing the closure under its feet. It
    never crashed, which is why it lasted; AddressSanitizer reports it on
    this suite's own re-entrancy tests. The callback is held on the stack for
    the duration of the call. No allocation per event, no layout change.

 -- Marius Schumacher <marius.schumacher@phisys.com>  Tue, 08 Sep 2026 09:54:48 +0200

